 the words እግዚኦ፡ መሐረነ፡ (thrice, e.g., fol. 92rb,
                           ll.5-6); 
 quire numbers or their elements.
 Calendar notes
                           concerning occasions for celebrating the given Anaphora (e.g., fols. 71rb
                           ll.1-3; 98vb ll.9-10) are written with alternating black and red
                           letters.</seg>
